====\\nQUALITY INTELLIGENCE\\n==================================\\n\\nQIS: 68.89\\n\\nEpic Coverage Score: 80.00\\nDefect Score (quality score, not bug ratio): 22.22\\nFeedback: 100.00\\nIncident Stability: 57.14\\n\\n==================================\\nSONAR QUALITY\\n==================================\\n\\nSonar Quality: 75.25\\n\\nBugs: 4\\nVulnerabilities: 1\\nCode Smells: 35\\nSonar Coverage: 72.5\\nDuplication: 4.3\\n\\n==================================\\nREQUIREMENT TRACEABILITY\\n==================================\\n\\nRequirements Total: 5\\nCovered Requirements: 4\\nUncovered Requirements: 1\\n\\n==================================\\nDEFECT INFORMATION\\n==================================\\n\\nStories: 9\\nTotal Bugs: 7\\nBug Ratio (bugs per 100 stories): 77.77777777777777\\n\\n==================================\\nEXPECTED ANALYSIS\\n==================================\\n\\nExplain why the deterministic release decision\\nis appropriate using only the supplied metrics.\\n\\nIdentify the most important quality risks.\\n\\nRank the recommended QA actions by priority.\\n\\nDo not calculate a new QIS.\\n\\nDo not change the supplied release decision.\\n\\nDo not invent missing metrics.\\n\\nQA_METRICS_CATALOG (definitions only; official Java values take precedence):\\n{\\"catalogVersion\\":\\"QA_METRICS_V2\\",\\"metrics\\":{\\"bugRatio\\":{\\"formula\\":\\"(totalBugs / totalStories) * 100\\",\\"unit\\":\\"bugs per 100 stories\\",\\"interpretation\\":\\"Higher means more reported bugs relative to user stories.\\"},\\"defectScore\\":{\\"formula\\":\\"100 - bugRatio\\",\\"unit\\":\\"quality score (not a defect percentage)\\",\\"interpretation\\":\\"Lower score indicates weaker quality in the defect dimension under this formula.\\"},\\"confidence\\":{\\"interpretation\\":\\"An application-specific indicator; its computation and meaning must be verified against Java implementation.\\"},\\"riskLevel\\":{\\"interpretation\\":\\"Use the exact value supplied by Java; do not downgrade or contradict it.\\"},\\"releaseDecision\\":{\\"interpretation\\":\\"Use the exact decision supplied by Java and describe the residual risks.\\"},\\"totalBugs\\":{\\"interpretation\\":\\"Reported total bug count used by the relevant QA metric.\\"},\\"bugs\\":{\\"interpretation\\":\\"Static analysis bug findings; verify provenance of the field.\\"},\\"codeSmells\\":{\\"interpretation\\":\\"Static-analysis maintainability findings.\\"},\\"uncoveredRequirements\\":{\\"interpretation\\":\\"Requirements not covered according to the application's coverage mapping.\\"},\\"coverageScore\\":{\\"formula\\":\\"(coveredEpics / totalEpics) * 100\\",\\"unit\\":\\"percent\\",\\"coverageRule\\":\\"An Epic is covered if it has at least one Story and every Story is Done. An Epic with zero Stories is NOT covered.\\"},\\"incidentScore\\":{\\"formula\\":\\"100 - incidentRate\\",\\"unit\\":\\"quality score on a nominal 0–100 scale\\"},\\"feedbackScore\\":{\\"formula\\":\\"100 if count(customer incidents with severity BLOCKER or CRITICAL) == 0 else 0\\",\\"unit\\":\\"binary quality score (0 or 100)\\"},\\"sonarScore\\":{\\"formula\\":\\"0.35 * sonarBugSubscore + 0.30 * sonarVulnerabilitySubscore + 0.20 * sonarCodeSmellSubscore + 0.15 * sonarDuplicationSubscore\\"},\\"businessQis\\":{\\"formula\\":\\"sum((configuredWeight_i / sumConfiguredWeights) * businessScore_i) over coverage, defect, feedback, incident, rca\\"},\\"qisFinal\\":{\\"formula\\":\\"0.80 * businessQis + 0.20 * sonarScore\\"}}}\\n", "totalStories": 9, "coverageScore": 80.0, "feedbackScore": 100.0, "incidentScore": 57.14, "sonarCoverage": 72.5, "releaseDecision": "GO_WITH_RISK", "vulnerabilities": 1, "totalRequirements": 5, "agentPolicyVersion": "QA_AGENT_POLICY_V3_1", "sourceSystemPrompt": "AGENT GOVERNANCE VERSION: QA_AGENT_POLICY_V3_1\\nMETRIC CATALOG VERSION: QA_METRICS_V2\\n\\nJava values and decisions are authoritative. Catalog defines semantics. Never invent evidence, severity or impact. Confidence is n