 Level: HIGH\\nMain Risk: DEFECT_QUALITY\\nConfidence: 95%\\n\\nQUALITY INTELLIGENCE\\n\\nQIS: 68.89\\n\\nEpic Coverage Score: 80.00\\nDefect Score (quality score, not bug ratio): 22.22\\nFeedback: 100.00\\nIncident Stability: 57.14\\n\\nSONAR QUALITY\\n\\nSonar Quality: 75.25\\n\\nBugs: 4\\nVulnerabilities: 1\\nCode Smells: 35\\nSonar Coverage: 72.5\\nDuplication: 4.3\\n\\nREQUIREMENT TRACEABILITY\\n\\nRequirements Total: 5\\nCovered Requirements: 4\\nUncovered Requirements: 1\\n\\nDEFECT INFORMATION\\n\\nStories: 9\\nTotal Bugs: 7\\nBug Ratio (bugs per 100 stories): 77.77777777777777\\n\\nEXPECTED ANALYSIS\\n\\nDescribe residual risks without claiming the decision is safe.\\n\\nIdentify the most important quality risks.\\n\\nRank the recommended QA actions by priority.\\n\\nDo not calculate a new QIS.\\n\\nDo not change the supplied release decision.\\n\\nDo not invent missing metrics.\\n\\nMetric definitions (Java values authoritative):\\ndefectScore: 100 - bugRatio Lower score indicates weaker quality in the defect dimension under this formula. \\nbugRatio: (totalBugs / totalStories) * 100 Higher means more reported bugs relative to user stories. \\nconfidence:  An application-specific indicator; its computation and meaning must be verified against Java implementation. \\ncoverageScore: (coveredEpics / totalEpics) * 100  An Epic is covered if it has at least one Story and every Story is Done. An Epic with zero Stories is NOT covered.\\nfeedbackScore: 100 if count(customer incidents with severity BLOCKER or CRITICAL) == 0 else 0  \\nincidentScore: 100 - incidentRate  \\n", "totalStories": 9, "coverageScore": 80.0, "feedbackScore": 100.0, "incidentScore": 57.14, "sonarCoverage": 72.5, "releaseDecision": "GO_WITH_RISK", "vulnerabilities": 1, "totalRequirements": 5, "agentPolicyVersion": "QA_AGENT_POLICY_V3_3", "sourceSystemPrompt": "AGENT GOVERNANCE VERSION: QA_AGENT_POLICY_V3_3\\nMETRIC CATALOG VERSION: QA_METRICS_V2\\n\\nJava values and decisions are authoritativ